# Sinfonia No. 1 in C major, BWV 787 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: bright and flowing. The subject is a rising sixteenth-note
# scale that keeps returning, in many keys and also turned upside down,
# over a walking bass. No big sectional breaks; the music runs on.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 80. Recording timings for the 21 bars: Andras Schiff
# (clavichord, ECM) 1:08, about 74 bpm; Angela Hewitt 0:57, about 88;
# Glenn Gould (1964) 0:46, about 110, which is too quick for the chip.
# 80 sits between Schiff and Hewitt: unhurried, the scales still run.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score, bars from 1):
#   1-7    exposition in C: subject top 1, mid 2, bottom 3, bottom
#          again 5; a light close in C at bar 7.
#   7-13   modulating: inverted scales lead to G (bars 7-9) and a
#          brief close in E minor (bar 10, beat 3); subject top 12 and
#          mid 13 in D minor; perfect cadence in D minor at bar 13.
#   14-16  entries in F (bottom 14), bottom 15, mid 16, turning home.
#   17-21  arrival on C with a flat-seventh (subdominant colour) at 17,
#          last bass entry at 19, final cadence 20-21.
# The E minor close at bar 10 is my own harmonic reading, not sourced.

tempo 80
rit 2 0.7                 # bars 20-21: the final cadence and held chord

dyn 1 mf                  # bars 1-10: the exposition, full tone
dyn 11 mp                 # bars 11-13: minor-key middle, after the E minor close
dyn 14 mf                 # bars 14-16: after the D minor cadence, entries in F
dyn 17 f                  # bars 17-21: home key, last entry and close

lead 1 top                # bar 1: subject in the top
lead 2 mid                # bar 2: answer in the middle
lead 3 bottom             # bar 3: subject in the bass
lead 5 bottom             # bar 5: bass entry again
lead 12 top               # bar 12: subject in D minor, top
lead 13 mid               # bar 13: subject in D minor, middle
lead 14-15 bottom         # bars 14-15: bass entries (F, then toward C)
lead 16 mid               # bar 16: middle entry
lead 19 bottom            # bar 19: last entry, in the bass, into the cadence
